Preserve UML host-failure provenance at the substrate boundary

Lost stubs, host termination signals, address-space setup failures and failed
stub handoffs abandon execution with the reserved infrastructure status. The
host-failure primitive is async-signal-safe and deliberately bypasses guest
panic notifiers and cleanup that could emit guest events. The launcher owns
process-group cleanup after observing the status. Guest-generated traps retain
their guest signal path; a failed host transport does not.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository kernel-patch
exception.

